      "id": "m1",
      "title": "CSV parser and object mapper",
      "status": "done",
      "plan": "## Objective\nImplement `parseCsv(text)` and `toObjects(rows)` in `src/csv.js`.\n\n## Requirements\n- `parseCsv` returns an array of rows, each row an array of strings.\n- Fields separated by commas.\n- A field wrapped in double quotes may contain commas and line breaks; `\"\"` inside it means one double quote.\n- Lines end with `\\n` or `\\r\\n`. A final line break does not add an empty row. Empty text gives `[]`.\n- `toObjects(rows)` uses the first row as header and returns one object per remaining row keyed by header, with missing columns filled with empty strings.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `npm test` passes.\n- Tests cover each bullet above, including quoted commas/newlines, doubled quotes, CRLF, trailing newline, empty input, and short rows.",
      "preview": null,
      "dispatch": null,
